From 08eab1da3c4199ae80da288065830048ad70fc57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:40:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(app): an op whose verdict reads the program ahead
 digests it in its stamp

Verify's prior acquittal (#96) and the turned family's pilot and facing
credits (#103) read the setup's earlier ops, but only Pocket3D and Drill
stamps digested them: a contour acquitted by a face kept reading Ok
after the face was regenerated shallower, and a bore kept its pilot's
credit after the pilot was deleted - both posted.

Every op with no 3+2 frame (exactly the set that collects verify's
prior plan) now writes the existing rest digest into its stamp
(drill_prior::reads_prior), so editing, regenerating, deleting or
reordering an earlier op of its setup marks it Stale and the post gate
refuses it; stale_reason names the moved predecessor. A posed op keeps
its stamp bit for bit.

One-time churn: every non-first unposed op of a saved project reads
Stale once and clears on regenerate. RegenerateAll converges in two
rounds when a later op reads an earlier one (the M3.1 C law Pocket3D
already ran on); the operations suite's batch test now says so.

turning_bore's fixture moved to tests/common/bore.rs to keep the suite
under the 400-line law.

Pinned by a_face_regenerated_shallower_marks_the_acquitted_contour_stale
(vertical_rapid_stock) and
a_pilot_deleted_or_made_shallower_after_the_bore_marks_it_stale
(turning_bore); both fail before the fix.

Fixes #109

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
