From 342bd44ad4d29e1523d941edd6edb8350042ca00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:54:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(app): one Regenerate All converges a job whose ops
 read the program ahead

Since the stamp digests the ops ahead (previous commit), a batch staged
against one frozen world stamped a dependent against its predecessor's
OLD path: one click left it Stale, a second click cleared it.

RegenerateAll now runs rounds in its constructor: each stages every
Stale op in program order, finishes them on rayon (M5.3 B), and writes
its results so the next round reads them; it stops when nothing is
Stale, capped at the op count, and names any op still Stale in
`skipped`. Every write is inverted before construction ends, so apply
replays the whole batch as ONE undo unit. `regenerated()` counts
distinct ops.

regenerate_all_fixes_the_whole_job_in_one_undo_unit expects one round
again; remachining's two-round test now converges in one
(a_params_edit_converges_in_one_regenerate_all); the threaded-batch
determinism test compares against the ordered apply-as-you-go loop.
Pinned by one_regenerate_all_brings_a_dependent_pair_current
(vertical_rapid_stock), which fails without this change.

Fixes #109
Fixes #145

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
