From 5cfeaf73aee2f8de3a55d6e0aca2ba49ad764673 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:15:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] perf(app): the program-ahead digest reads a path
 signature stored at the write

#153 review B1: since #109 every unposed op's stamp digests the ops
ahead, and the digest cloned and hashed each predecessor's whole
toolpath - inside status_of, which the status bar and the browser ask
for every op every frame (M^2 path clones per frame).

schema::Toolpath now carries a private signature (path_sig::of, the old
rest::path_hash) computed in Toolpath::new, its only constructor; the
digest and the stale story read it through a borrowed component and
clone nothing. Only the prior plan and the pilot credit, which cut the
grid, still copy moves.

Review N3: the predecessor's kind tag joins the digest (the prior plan
and the pilot credit branch on it). N1: a Regenerate All round defers
an op that reads the program ahead when an op ahead of it in its setup
is staged in that round, so each op generates once.

Pinned by the_program_ahead_digest_moves_only_with_the_path,
a_reorder_marks_the_dependent_stale and
a_posed_op_keeps_its_stamp_when_the_program_ahead_moves
(vertical_rapid_stock).

Refs #109
Refs #145

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
