From bc8324f56c5039c9c504d049dfd4ea3352ac5aae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:23:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(app): a refused op ahead no longer holds back the ops
 Regenerate All deferred behind it

#153 re-review: the rounds loop stopped on a round with no successful
results, so when an op ahead staged and its generator refused, every
dependent deferred behind it in that round was never regenerated and
was misreported as "still stale after N round(s)".

The loop now stops only when a round staged nothing. A refusal is final
(the op is in `skipped` and excluded from later rounds), so the ops it
held back run next round against the world as it stands. The leftover
message counts the rounds actually run.

Pinned by a_refused_op_ahead_does_not_hold_back_the_ops_behind_it
(vertical_rapid_stock): a staged face whose clearance the grown stock
overtops refuses by name; the contour behind it is regenerated and
judged, and is the only op regenerated.

Refs #145

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
